    helpWater: "Outdoor › Pond digs a natural basin into the ground with a level water surface (water height above the lowest rim point, bed depth). Stream is drawn as a line (click the points, double-click or Enter ends) with a width: a muddy bed along the line and water following the slope.",
    helpNotes: "Objects › Note pins a text note on any surface: wall, floor, roof, ground or object. Pins follow the camera, show a number, the text and a done box; the list has a Notes group, the panel edits text, colour, done and position. The 2D plan draws the notes of the storey as numbered circles with a legend.",
    helpKeys: "Keys: 1–8 tabs · V select · letters in parentheses on buttons (menu N/O/S/X/I/P, view G/C/B/J/Q/T/K/F, modes W/E/R/M, tools A/L/U/Z per tab, Note U, Kitchen L) · [ ] rotate ghost · Enter close area · Ctrl+Z/Y · Ctrl+D · Delete · Walk: WASD · Esc · ? help",
    room: "Room", rooms: "Rooms", area: "Area", grossArea: "Gross area", perimeter: "Perimeter", floorFinish: "Floor finish", ceiling: "Ceiling",
    roomHint: "Rooms are detected from closed wall loops; the name and finishes follow the room when its walls move.", roomDerived: "Rooms come from the walls: move or delete a wall instead.",
    quantities: "Quantities…", quantitiesTitle: "Quantities", quantitiesCsv: "Quantities (CSV)", pcs: "pcs", site: "Site", item: "Item", quantity: "Quantity", unit: "Unit", materialCol: "Material", noQuantities: "Nothing to count yet.",
    cat_rooms: "Rooms (area)", cat_walls: "Walls (length)", cat_wallFacesInner: "Wall faces, inner", cat_wallFacesOuter: "Wall faces, outer", cat_floors: "Floors", cat_roof: "Roof", cat_siteWalls: "Boundary walls", cat_outdoor: "Decks, pools, paths", cat_garden: "Garden patches", cat_railings: "Railings", cat_fences: "Fences", cat_doors: "Doors", cat_windows: "Windows", cat_gates: "Gates", cat_stairs: "Stairs", cat_objects: "Objects",
    helpRooms: "Rooms: every area closed by walls on a storey is a room, listed under the storey with its net area (inside the wall faces). Select a room in the list or by its label in the 3D view to name it and give it a floor texture or colour and a ceiling colour; the name follows the room when its walls move. The 📏 Measures button shows and hides the room labels.",
    helpQuantities: "Project › Quantities opens a bill of quantities per building and storey: wall lengths and face areas by material (inner and outer), floor and roof areas, room areas, boundary walls, decks, pools, paths and patches, railings and fences, doors, windows and gates by type, stairs and objects by catalog name. Quantities (CSV) downloads the same table.",
